# Firebase Configuration
# Replace with your actual Firebase config values
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your_project_id.firebaseapp.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your_project_id
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=your_project_id.appspot.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=your_messaging_sender_id
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=your_app_id

# Instructions:
# 1. Go to https://console.firebase.google.com/
# 2. Create a new project or select existing one
# 3. Enable Authentication
# 4. Enable Google and Email/Password sign-in methods
# 5. Add Discord as a custom OAuth provider (coming soon)
# 6. Copy your config values from Project Settings > General > Your apps
# 7. Rename this file to .env.local
# 8. Replace the placeholder values with your actual Firebase config
